index 9f4db5bac6..251c90138a 100644
--- a/CLAUDE.md
+++ b/CLAUDE.md
@@ -43,7 +43,7 @@ Build prerequisites and gotchas:
 
 This is a Poetry repo. Sibling `submission-schema` migrated to `uv`; do not confuse the two.
 
-- **Use poetry 2.4.1 or 2.4.3.** CI pins 2.4.1 in every workflow (`pipx install poetry==2.4.1`). The `poetry.lock` content-hash is poetry-version-sensitive: a different poetry version can report the lock as "out of sync with pyproject.toml" even when the dependencies are unchanged. 2.4.3 was checked against `main` on 2026-09-15: `poetry check --lock` reports "All set!", and `poetry lock` leaves the committed lock byte-identical. For any other version, run `poetry check --lock` before trusting it, and align dev/container poetry to one of these two. CI runs `poetry check` (in `main.yaml`) to catch real pyproject/lock drift in PRs rather than on a teammate's fresh install. To sync after editing pyproject: `poetry lock` (no `--regenerate` unless you intend to bump versions).
+- **Use poetry 2.4.3.** CI pins it in every workflow (`pipx install poetry==2.4.3`). The `poetry.lock` content-hash is poetry-version-sensitive: a different poetry version can report the lock as "out of sync with pyproject.toml" even when the dependencies are unchanged. With 2.4.3 against `main` on 2026-09-15, `poetry check --lock` reports "All set!" and `poetry lock` leaves the committed lock byte-identical. For any other version, run `poetry check --lock` before trusting it, and align dev/container poetry to 2.4.3. CI runs `poetry check` (in `main.yaml`) to catch real pyproject/lock drift in PRs rather than on a teammate's fresh install. To sync after editing pyproject: `poetry lock` (no `--regenerate` unless you intend to bump versions).
 
 - Never create a `uv.lock` here, and never run `uv add`, `uv sync`, or `uv lock`. If a stray `uv.lock` appears, delete it before committing.
 - Before tightening any pin in `pyproject.toml` (especially `linkml`), check that `submission-schema` still resolves. nmdc-schema is a library, so a tighter pin propagates to consumers even when nmdc-schema itself does not exercise the feature. `linkml` and `linkml-runtime` versions must be paired (a runtime release can drop something the matching `linkml` references).
